    "title": "Jacques-André Istel plans to offer heralded museum as a 'gift to the nation'",
    "text": "Jacques-André Istel plans to make The Museum of History in Granite – a storied landmark in Felicity, California – “a substantial and permanent gift to the nation.” Istel owns the museum in partnership with his wife Felicia. The site is 17 miles west of Yuma.\nThe museum contains more than 700 granite panels apportioned to various monuments, and it harbors a range of other features, as well. One of the most striking structures is a sundial fashioned in the form of the “Arm of God” – a reference to Michelangelo’s fresco, “The Creation of Adam,” in the Sistine Chapel.",
    "summary": "Jacques-André Istel plans to make The Museum of History in Granite – a storied landmark in Felicity, California – “a substantial and permanent gift to the nation.” Istel owns the museum in partnership with his wife Felicia. The site is 17 miles west of Yuma. The museum contains more than 700 granite panels apportioned to various monuments, and it harbors a range of other features, as well. One of the most striking structures is a sundial fashioned in the form of the “Arm of God” – a reference to Michelangelo’s fresco, “The Creation of Adam,” in the Sistine Chapel.",
